{"title":"Math competition books","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>These <b>math competition books</b> are collections of problems for specific individual <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">mathematics competitions</a>.  Compilations of problems at a single level from multiple competitions can be found in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">math books</a> page or elsewhere. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> books, while not devoted specifically to contest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problem_solving\" title=\"Problem solving\">problem solving</a>, contain scores of problems from the contests listed below, as well as others, and are great preparation for those contests.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Elementary_School\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Elementary School</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Collegiate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elementary_School\">Elementary School</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Elementary School\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_Olympiads_for_Elementary_and_Middle_Schools\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematical Olympiads for Elementary and Middle Schools\">Mathematical Olympiads for Elementary and Middle Schools</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MOEMS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"MOEMS\">MOEMS</a>) publishes <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/moems-olympiad3\">an excellent contest problem book</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ap1\">Australia Primary Contest book 1</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ap2\">Australia Primary Contest book 2</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_League\" title=\"Math League\">Math League</a> sells its collections of elementary school contests <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.mathleague.com/index.php/online-store/contest-books-grades-4-6-grades-7-8-algebra-1-high-school/36-mathleaguewebsite/shopping/52-grades-45-and-6-contest-books\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0521585686/artofproblems-20\">More Mathematical Challenges</a> by Tony Gardiner.  Over 150 problems from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=UK_Junior_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"UK Junior Mathematical Olympiad\">UK Junior Mathematical Olympiad</a>, for students ages 11-15.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ab1\">Australia 1978-84 (PDF)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ab2\">Australia 1985-91 (PDF)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ab3\">Australia 1992-98 (softcover)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ab4\">Australia 1999-2005 (PDF)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/ab5\">Australia 2006-12 (softcover)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/B0B2TD8H4X/artofproblems-20\">Central Wisconsin Math League</a> problems and solutions.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_League\" title=\"Math League\">Math League</a> sells its grades 7 and 8 (including Algebra 1) contest collections <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.mathleague.com/index.php/online-store/contest-books-grades-4-6-grades-7-8-algebra-1-high-school/36-mathleaguewebsite/shopping/53-grades-7-and-8-contest-books\">here</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_League\" title=\"Math League\">Math League</a> sells its High School contest collections <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.mathleague.com/index.php/online-store/contest-books-grades-4-6-grades-7-8-algebra-1-high-school/36-mathleaguewebsite/shopping/50-highschoolcontestbooks\">here</a>.</li>\n<li>While the problems aren't past contest problems, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0578572389/artofproblems-20\">Challenging Problems in Middle School Math</a> contains 10 practice contests for the AMC 8.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mandelbrot_Competition\" title=\"Mandelbrot Competition\">Mandelbrot Competition</a> has <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/store/list/other-products#Mandelbrot\">two problem books for sale</a> at <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a>.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ARML\">ARML</a> books are linked on <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//arml3.com/arml-books/\">this page</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/17\">USA and International Mathematical Olympiads 2005</a> by Zuming Feng, Melanie Matchett Wood, and Cecil Rousseau.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/11\">Mathematical Olympiads 2000-2001: Problems and Solutions from Around the World</a> by Titu Andreescu, Zuming Feng, and George Lee Jr.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4419-9854-5\">The IMO Compendium: A Collection of Problems Suggested for The International Mathematical Olympiads: 1959-2004</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=NML/42\">Hungarian Problem Book III</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/23\">Hungarian Problem Book IV</a></li>\n<li>Collections of Olympiads by the Australian Mathematics Trust\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/apo\">APMO 1989-2000</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/usr\">USSR 1989-1992</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/amo1\">Australia 1979-1995</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/amo2\">Australia 1996-2011 (PDF)</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/amo3\">Australia 2012-2019 (PDF), also includes AMOC Senior Contests from that time</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/cmo1\">China 1981-93</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/cmo2\">China 1993-2001</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/cmo3\">China 2001-2009</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/pao\">Poland and Austria 1981-1995</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/hi\">Hungary-Israeli Math Competition 1990-2001</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/bmc\">Bulgaria 1992-2001</a></li>\n<li>Tournament of Towns collections: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt1\">Book 1 (1980-84)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt2\">Book 2 (1984-89)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt3\">Book 3 (1989-93)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt4\">Book 4 (1993-97)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt5\">Book 5 (1997-2002)</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://shop.amt.edu.au/products/tt6\">Book 6 (2002-2007)</a></li></ul></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.awesomemath.org/product/balkan-mathematical-olympiads/\">Balkan Mathematical Olympiads</a> by Mircea Becheanu and Bogdan Enescu.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.awesomemath.org/product/a-romanian-problem-book/\">A Romanian Problem Book</a> by Titu Andreescu and Marian Tetiva.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9814289590/artofproblems-20\">Selected Problems Of The Vietnamese Mathematical Olympiad (1962-2009)</a> by Hai Chau Le and Hai Khoi Le.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9814390216/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2009-2010): Problems And Solutions</a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9813142936/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2011-2014): Problems And Solutions</a> by Xiong Bin and Lee Peng Yee</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9811251916/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2015-2016): Problems And Solutions</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9811257388/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2017-2018): Problems And Solutions</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9811257396/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2019-2020): Problems And Solutions</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9811284547/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2021-2022): Problems And Solutions</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9819808480/artofproblems-20\">Mathematical Olympiad In China (2023): Problems And Solutions</a>, all by Xiong Bin</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=MCL/4\">Moscow Mathematical Olympiads, 1993-1999</a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=MCL/7\">Moscow Mathematical Olympiads, 2000-2005</a> by Roman Federov, Alexei Belov, Alexander Kovaldzhi, and Ivan Yashchenko.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.routledge.com/Puzzle-and-Proof-A-Decade-of-Problems-from-the-Utah-Math-Olympiad/Dittmer-Golze-Molnar-Stanford/p/book/9781032755526\">Puzzle and Proof: A Decade of Problems from the Utah Math Olympiad</a> by Samuel Dittmer, Hiram Golze, Grant Molnar, and Caleb Stanford.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-387-75472-7\">The Colorado Mathematical Olympiad and Further Explorations: From the Mountains of Colorado to the Peaks of Mathematics</a> by Alexander Soifer.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-319-52861-8\">The Colorado Mathematical Olympiad: The Third Decade and Further Explorations</a> by Alexander Soifer.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//store.doverpublications.com/products/9780486277097\">The USSR Olympiad Problem Book</a> by D.O. Shklarsky, N. N. Chentzov, and I. M. Yaglom.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9811254974/artofproblems-20\">Leningrad Mathematical Olympiads (1961-1991)</a> newer, better, cheaper version of the 1987-1991 book with more problems and much better solutions. Aside from all the Leningrad Olympiad problems, it also contains 120 additional problems.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/8\">A Friendly Mathematics Competition: Thirty-Five Years of Teamwork in Indiana</a> by Rick Gillman covers 35 years of the Indiana College Mathematics Competition.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//store.doverpublications.com/products/9780486151823\">The Red Book of Mathematical Problems</a> by Kenneth S. Williams and Kenneth Hardy has 100 Putnam-level problems.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/32\">Putnam 1938-64</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/30\">1965-84</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/33\">1985-2000</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=PRB/37\">2001-16</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4612-0733-7\">Contests in Higher Mathematics</a> by Gabor J. Szekely. Contains problems from the 1962-1991 Miklos Schweitzer competitions.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_competition_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">Math books</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks\" title=\"Math textbooks\">Math textbooks</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Resources_for_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Resources for mathematics competitions\">Resources for mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Academic_competitions\" title=\"Academic competitions\">Academic competitions</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018094257\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 62/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1522:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018094257 and revision id 285687. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}